{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-n0001108","units":[{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"The source identifies the interaction core as an interaction among three agents.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"The source states that this three-agent interaction core has the one-step diamond property.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"The one-step diamond property means that when two one-step interactions start from the same state, each resulting state can take one additional interaction to reach the same state.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-n0001109","units":[{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"For nonlinear systems, the paper claims Church-Rosser confluence only after canonicalization and a global schedule are added.","requires":["Church-Rosser confluence","canonicalization","global schedule"],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"For nonlinear systems, the paper claims optimality only after canonicalization and a global schedule are added.","requires":["optimality","canonicalization","global schedule"],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Church-Rosser confluence means that different valid interaction or rewrite sequences can be continued until they reach a common result.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Canonicalization converts equivalent representations into one chosen canonical form, while a global schedule constrains the interaction order across the whole system.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-n0001110","units":[{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"Δ-Nets aims to represent each sharing context with a variable-arity replicator.","requires":["sharing context","variable-arity replicator"],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"mechanism","basis":"source","text":"Δ-Nets uses local interactions and limited global discipline to avoid preventable work.","requires":["local interactions","global discipline"],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Variable arity means that an operation can handle different numbers of connections or copies instead of one fixed number.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"A sharing context is a computation context in which one value, resource, or structure is used by multiple consumers.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false},{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Local interactions update directly connected components, whereas global discipline coordinates behavior across a wider system when needed.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]}]}
